author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "A read whose rows were dropped for a token budget discloses the binding budget, its source, and a recovery instruction that works on that command; The disclosure names any explicitly requested dimension the budget overrode, so a caller can tell a downgraded request from an exhausted result set; has_more true is never emitted without either a usable continuation cursor or a named alternative recovery path; A regression test drives a real workspace read past the default ceiling and asserts the disclosure, rather than asserting only that truncation occurred; The row-compaction path and the whole-result omission path disclose recovery through the same declared shape"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Attached a machine-readable truncation disclosure at the point where the binding budget and resolved dimensions are both in scope, reporting precedence inversion as data rather than prose."
expected_result: "A read whose rows were dropped for a token budget states the budget, what it overrode, and how to obtain the complete result."
actual_result: "output_budget_truncation reports reason, budget_source default, budget_tokens 6000, overridden_dimensions [amount], and a restore_with naming --output-budget unbounded and the paging alternative."
